# Deploy Receipt Log
# Format: <ISO8601> | path=<prod-path> | sha=<git-sha> | route=<sftp|scp|script> | lane=<agent-id>
# Append-only. Committed to the repo so all lanes can read it.
#
# This file is NOT a replacement for git history — it records the publish event
# (who, when, how), which git author fields cannot answer: 252 of 289 commits on
# origin/main carry a synthesised ^pehonong@<host>\.local$ address that names nobody
# (derive it, don't read this number: measured 2026-09-17).
#
# Route values:
#   script  = deploy.sh (rsync + sshpass)
#   scp     = manual scp upload
#   sftp    = manual SFTP upload
#
# 🔴 COVERAGE LIMIT — READ BEFORE TREATING AN ABSENT ROW AS AN ABSENT DEPLOY.
# scripts/deploy.sh is the ONLY writer in this repo, and it hardcodes route=script.
# `scp` and `sftp` are documented above but CANNOT be produced: nothing outside
# deploy.sh appends here. So this ledger instruments the one route that already
# leaves a git sha, and is structurally blind to the two routes that don't —
# which are the routes every unattributed prod post took (d31cca9, 7ece2bb,
# fb153ab, 2b41803). A quiet ledger is the expected reading for a manual upload,
# not evidence one didn't happen.
#
# As of 2026-09-17 this file has ZERO data rows and has never been written by a
# deploy. Created 11:34, seeded by fcdb0c3, untouched since. Absence here proves
# nothing about production.
#
# See spec: ~/.openclaw-kilokaki/workspace/specs/deploy-receipt.md
